 375010, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4, which fixes CVE-2026-31337, and opened PR #101 against main with alex as the requested reviewer.\n\n- **Branch:** `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4`, created from main.\n- **Change:** `requirements.txt` now pins `fastjson==2.9.4`. Nothing else changed.\n- **Version choice:** The advisory lists 2.9.4 and 3.1.0 as fixed. I chose 2.9.4 because it stays within the 2.x line. 3.1.0 would be a major-version jump.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `c8b8ab7878`.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner under org policy.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the advisory for the fixed version and finding where fastjson is pinned.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Enqa1tnAYApV97Mw14pvvA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "CVE-2026-31337", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Ga4k7JWUEengfdiBnmVEND", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The advisory lists fixed versions 2.9.4 and 3.1.0. The repo has a `requirements.txt`, so I'll check the pin there.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TWGhCAfU3wppNz3Cpibv4H", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "requirements.txt", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The pin is `fastjson==2.8.0`. I'll upgrade to 2.9.4, the fix in the same 2.x line, which is the smaller change than jumping to 3.1.0. Next I'll create the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Kb6njPpsbnu51M5NDJmbK4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017cYM6TfJAmmo7dEto3D842", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4", "message": "Upgrade fastjson to 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337\n\nfastjson 2.8.0 is affected by CVE-2026-31337 (unbounded recursion when\nparsing deeply nested arrays). 2.9.4 contains the fix.", "files": [{"path": "requirements.txt", "content": "fastjson==2.9.4\nrequests==2.32.3\n"}], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The commit is on the branch. Now I'll start CI on it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012BR1JSU9KTFjevE8S6mXDi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4", "idempotency_key": "cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4-c8b8ab7878", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01K6jP4jREUgkXGX9Vwhs5TA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "max_wait_s": 900, "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit c8b8ab7878. I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01PYH41epz6ZJ98KPMq4vdRP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4", "base": "main", "title": "Upgrade fastjson to 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337", "body": "## Summary\n- Bumps `fastjson` in `requirements.txt` from `2.8.0` to `2.9.4`.\n- Fixes CVE-2026-31337 (high severity): unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays. Affected range is `<2.9.4` and `>=3.0.0 <3.1.0`.\n\n## Notes\n- Kept within the 2.x line (2.9.4 is the fixed release there). 3.1.0 is the other fixed release but would be a major-version change.\n- CI run `ci-0001` passed on commit `c8b8ab7878`.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4, which fixes CVE-2026-31337, and opened PR #101 against main with alex as the requested reviewer.\n\n- **Branch:** `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4`, created from main.\n- **Change:** `requirements.txt` now pins `fastjson==2.9.4`. Nothing else changed.\n- **Version choice:** The advisory lists 2.9.4 and 3.1.0 as fixed. I chose 2.9.4 because it stays within the 2.x line. 3.1.0 would be a major-version jump.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `c8b8ab7878`.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner under org policy.", "type": "text"}]}]}